39534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440960 1071 "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}{x}^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [0,4].$" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440960 1072 #uuid "6cce7317-466a-565b-96aa-fdea6ef81a13" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440960 1074 "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between two points where $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula:\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}{x}^{3/2},$ $a=0,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\sqrt{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=\\sqrt{2x}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[\\sqrt{2x}]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=1+2x.$ Then, $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$\n\nWe also need to compute new limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 4 \\\\ u & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}]|}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({9}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27-1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440961 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440958 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440961 1069 "q-85663" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440961 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440961 1071 "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{2}{3}(x-1)^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [1,4].$" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440961 1072 #uuid "b4cc4c19-d62f-5fe8-890e-23b350c71bdb" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440961 1074 "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}(x-1)^{3/2},$ $a=1,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(x-1)^{1/2}=\\sqrt{x-1}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\sqrt{x-1})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+x-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{x}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(8-1)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440962 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440959 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440962 1069 "q-82640" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440962 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440962 1071 "The length of the curve $y={cos}^{2}⁡x$ on $[0,\\pi ]$ is given by" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440962 1072 #uuid "e7f022af-185f-5ff9-8180-e7c6bb598640" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440962 1074 "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)={cos}^{2}⁡x,$ $a=0,$ and $b=\\pi .$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440963 1058 #edb/ref 17592186440966 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440963 1062 #uuid "452b2cbc-5117-5efd-9982-a18432f21445" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440963 1063 #edb/ref 17592186440962 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440964 1062 #uuid "68036def-8478-52cf-aa86-bdc7e9362873" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440964 1063 #edb/ref 17592186321050 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440965 1058 #edb/ref 17592186440964 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440965 1062 #uuid "e3745ff0-a922-503d-a4d2-94c9a8749582" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440965 1063 #edb/ref 17592186440961 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440966 1058 #edb/ref 17592186440965 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440966 1062 #uuid "ee3585d8-5f49-56ae-b07f-bde4ee96637e" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440966 1063 #edb/ref 17592186440960 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440967 1058 #edb/ref 17592186440963 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440967 1062 #uuid "efd64853-bb37-514e-befa-229e2804aefb" 13194139534851 17592186045417 true] [17592186440967 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083772 13194139534851 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-9b3ec084-e75c-5ee3-acd7-658c0b8e62d6" 17592186440941 "answer-135fa4af-c45b-5bcb-a835-dbd3b68255f6" 17592186440942 "answer-3282f6dd-ea0d-5250-b6a0-e1760944dcbc" 17592186440943 "answer-385be674-f982-5b0d-a246-7c05ff2eae39" 17592186440944 "answer-4c99b7f5-f882-59fc-acc5-121343a55257" 17592186440945 "answer-4e80d767-11f6-5557-956d-f161a62d1488" 17592186440946 "answer-628f8af6-109d-5b4d-ba07-98c8c66ae500" 17592186440947 "answer-6fade50c-3a34-568e-84e3-7d56cc0c5b4b" 17592186440948 "answer-874efc84-b50d-5b16-b1a0-a3259348480c" 17592186440949 "answer-87d8988f-ee76-5568-a61f-b92eb15fbc84" 17592186440950 "answer-b5a976e6-bf11-50a3-a22